Q("Store Credit is unavailable offline because:", ["It is rarely used", "The customer's balance lives on the server and cannot be verified from the terminal", "It is disabled by default", "Tax cannot compute"], 1, "A balance the till cannot check is a balance it will not spend.", "Ch3"),
Q("Allow Clear Cart off, plus an approver holding Clear Cart, means:", ["No Clear button at all", "The Clear button appears but requires an approval — discarding a basket becomes a recorded event", "Cashiers clear freely", "Carts lock permanently"], 1, "Relevant to the take-cash-then-clear fraud pattern.", "Ch4"),
Q("Auto Allocate Batch picks:", ["The newest batch", "Batches automatically, oldest first, asking only when the quantity cannot be covered", "Randomly", "By price"], 1, "Good for expiry-dated goods; off where the cashier should choose.", "Ch4"),
Q("Allow Negative Stock:", ["Is purely a profile choice", "Mirrors a company-wide stock setting and will not save unless that setting also allows it", "Is always on", "Only affects reports"], 1, "The profile cannot override company inventory policy.", "Ch4"),
Q("Offline login expires:", ["Never", "Seven days after the cashier's last successful online sign-in on that terminal", "Daily", "When the shift closes"], 1, "Why cashiers should sign in online at least weekly.", "Ch4"),
Q("Allow Transaction Date Edit is granted sparingly because:", ["It slows the till", "A back-dated sale moves revenue from one reporting day to another; future dates are never allowed", "It confuses customers", "It breaks receipts"], 1, "Reporting integrity behind one checkbox.", "Ch4"),
Q("The most consequential setting on the profile is:", ["The receipt footer", "Discount Mode — it decides how a cashier can reduce a price", "The search limit", "The kiosk flag"], 1, "Choose it deliberately, never by default.", "Ch5"),
Q("Approval-based mode requires every discount to carry:", ["A manager's signature", "A reason from the markdown list plus a typed explanation — neither can be blank", "A code", "A customer name"], 1, "Month-end reporting can then say why margin was given.", "Ch5"),
Q("In Code-based mode, the cashier:", ["Types discounts freely", "Cannot type a discount at all — they request one, and apply the single-use code a category lead approves", "Uses yesterday's codes", "Calls the MD"], 1, "The strongest control, at the cost of a round trip.", "Ch5"),
Q("One-time approval codes:", ["Go to one approver", "Are emailed to every approver holding the relevant permission, and expire after one hour", "Never expire", "Work offline"], 1, "The whole group sees every request — no quiet arrangements.", "Ch5"),
Q("Rate editing is stronger than discounting because:", ["It is faster", "A discount is limited by the price; a rate edit replaces the price itself — so mark it and require an override", "It skips tax", "It needs no marker"], 1, "Edited lines carry the Rate override marker.", "Ch5"),
Q("A line with a promotional discount:", ["Can be discounted further", "Is locked — no manual discount or rate change can be added on top", "Loses its promotion", "Doubles the discount"], 1, "Campaign discounts do not stack with manual ones.", "Ch5"),
